    "lesson": {
      "title": "Steel hull and block",
      "instruction": "Why can the same steel float as a watertight hollow hull?",
      "explanation": "Quasi-static still-water equilibrium for a sealed box hull and a solid block made from the same material mass and volume. Flooded interior excludes no water, so only material volume provides buoyancy. At full submersion equality is neutral equilibrium. No waves, surface tension or ship engineering."
